<title>MEXICO: Maseca indefinitely postpones announcement.</title>
<headline>Maseca indefinitely postpones announcement.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's corn flour producer Maseca on Wednesday indefinitely postponed a planned announcement it had been due to make about the corn subsidy system in Mexico.</p>
<p>&quot;It's postponed,&quot; a press official said. He was unable to give an explanation.</p>
<p>Earlier, Maseca issued a statement saying it was due to hold a news conference at 1345 local time (1845 GMT) &quot;to make...an important announcement about the system of subsidizing the purchase of corn in Mexico.&quot;</p>
<p>Mexico media have speculated that the government might be changing, or increasing, the ceiling on age-old subsidies on corn-flour, the key ingredient of tortillas.</p>
<p>Maseca is controlled by Gruma</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
